Pulse — Licensing Overview
==========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Oblivion Pictures — Michael de Meyer (https://howispulse.com)

Pulse is source-available, not open source. The source is published so that
anyone can read, audit and modify it, but the licences below place limits on
how it may be used. Two licences apply, depending on which part of the
repository a file belongs to.


1. Server components — PolyForm Free Trial 1.0.0
------------------------------------------------
Full text: LICENSE-SERVER.md

    services/
    shared/
    infra/
    Dockerfile.service
    docker-compose.yml
    pyproject.toml
    uv.lock

These are the components required to operate a Pulse server. You may evaluate
them for less than 32 consecutive days. Operating a Pulse server beyond that
requires a commercial licence from the copyright holder, regardless of whether
the deployment is commercial, private or non-profit.

Self-hosting is offered as a paid, activated service. See
https://howispulse.com for terms.


2. Client components — PolyForm Perimeter 1.0.0
-----------------------------------------------
Full text: LICENSE-CLIENT.md

    web/
    desktop/
    mobile/
    streaming/          (except streaming/patches/, see section 3)
    plugins/
    packaging/
    Logo/
    scripts/

These may be used and redistributed freely, including commercially. The only
prohibited use is providing a product that competes with Pulse.

Using the Pulse web app, desktop app or mobile app to connect to a Pulse
server — including the hosted service at howispulse.com — is unrestricted and
free of charge. No licence needs to be purchased to use Pulse as an end user.


3. Third-party components
-------------------------
Parts of this repository are not owned by the copyright holder and keep their
original licences:

    streaming/patches/              GPL-3.0-or-later
        Patches against gpu-screen-recorder. Derivative works of GPL-licensed
        source and therefore GPL-licensed themselves. The recorder itself is
        not contained in this repository; it is fetched at build time from
        https://repo.dec05eba.com/gpu-screen-recorder and bundled into the
        Linux package as a separate program.

    infra/mediamtx-fork/patches/    MIT
        Patches against MediaMTX (https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx).

    web/static/vendor/resonance-audio/      Apache-2.0
    web/static/sounds/                      CC0-1.0
    web/src/lib/components/ui/              MIT (shadcn-svelte, bits-ui)

Third-party dependencies resolved at build time (Python, Node and Rust
packages, FFmpeg) carry their own licences and are not relicensed by this
document.


